  "key_evidence": [
    "Why it matters: the federal agency that enforces workplace discrimination law is now suing this university. The EEOC filed suit on 12 August 2026 alleging Washington University in St. Louis eliminated an employee's job after she complained about race-based separation during a mandatory training.",
    "The complaint describes a nine-month sequence: internal complaint January 2025, EEOC charge July 2025, duties transferred away, position eliminated November 2025. This is an agency-filed allegation, NOT an adjudicated finding, and is scored as such.",
    "WashU eliminated 316 filled positions and 198 unfilled ones, saving about $52 million a year, and skipped merit raises for fiscal 2026. Local reporting records staff demanding to see how those decisions were made.",
    "Financial aid moved the other way: about $33 million more spent since June 2022, and the 2026-27 tuition rise held to 4.5%. Equity therefore holds at 3.00 rather than falling.",
    "Accountability falls to 2.20 of 5 and Integrity to 2.40 of 5. Nothing in the public record shows self-initiated acknowledgment, correction or repair."
  ],
